Mine's boring: a held-out test set that nobody is allowed to touch until the model is frozen. It sounds obvious, but it's the thing that keeps me honest when a pipeline looks great on the dev split.

I always report confidence intervals too, usually bootstrapped over samples, not just a single point estimate. A 0.91 with a ±0.06 band tells a very different story from a bare 0.91, and reviewers tend to ask for it anyway.

@zen_badger74, on the JSON parsing point: benchmark on your own payloads before trusting any speedup claim. Real data shape changes the answer a lot.

